WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.454
A list of names isn't a pipeline.

2
00:00:03.134 --> 00:00:05.694
Find leads with AI, then actually follow up.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.582
Give AI context once, then repeat three moves,

4
00:00:11.202 --> 00:00:13.183
find leads, verify the details,

5
00:00:13.542 --> 00:00:16.122
and organize the follow-up. What you learn

6
00:00:16.122 --> 00:00:17.342
shapes your next search.

7
00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:21.175
Start by teaching Gemini what you do and

8
00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:21.855
who you help.

9
00:00:22.575 --> 00:00:24.855
Here, I paste a short public business description

10
00:00:24.855 --> 00:00:26.795
and ask for an audience summary.

11
00:00:27.255 --> 00:00:28.835
You can do this without connecting your inbox.

12
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.609
Give the search a clear audience, location, and

13
00:00:34.609 --> 00:00:35.149
time window.

14
00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:38.369
Here it is small business owners, Houston or

15
00:00:38.369 --> 00:00:40.629
online, and November through January.

16
00:00:41.149 --> 00:00:42.969
Then ask why each opportunity fits.

17
00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:47.254
Notice the six parts of the prompt, a

18
00:00:47.254 --> 00:00:52.194
research role, a specific task, where, when, the

19
00:00:52.194 --> 00:00:52.654
workshop

20
00:00:52.654 --> 00:00:55.254
offer, and a table as the output.

21
00:00:55.794 --> 00:00:58.214
I also asked Gemini to flag anything it

22
00:00:58.214 --> 00:00:59.034
cannot verify.

23
00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.644
Next, research the gaps.

24
00:01:03.364 --> 00:01:06.984
A public contact path, an application link, a

25
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:09.944
pitch angle, and a concrete next action.

26
00:01:10.664 --> 00:01:12.664
A missing field should stay missing.

27
00:01:13.264 --> 00:01:16.044
These are candidates to review, not confirmed speaking

28
00:01:16.044 --> 00:01:16.544
invitations.

29
00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:19.595
Open the original source.

30
00:01:20.435 --> 00:01:22.915
The expo page confirms December 2nd,

31
00:01:23.115 --> 00:01:25.375
but the speaker application adds something important.

32
00:01:26.055 --> 00:01:28.695
It is unpaid, spots are not guaranteed,

33
00:01:29.415 --> 00:01:31.415
and applications fill last-minute openings.

34
00:01:32.255 --> 00:01:34.035
I correct the next action and keep the

35
00:01:34.035 --> 00:01:35.375
status as needs review.

36
00:01:36.355 --> 00:01:38.335
Gemini prepares. You approve.

37
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:42.836
Put the corrected leads into a simpler table.

38
00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.276
Give every row a status and a next

39
00:01:45.276 --> 00:01:45.716
action.

40
00:01:46.276 --> 00:01:49.016
Open the table menu, choose Export to Sheets,

41
00:01:49.396 --> 00:01:51.056
and open the spreadsheet when it is ready.

42
00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:56.168
Now make the tracker easy to use. Select

43
00:01:56.168 --> 00:01:57.988
the table and wrap the text.

44
00:01:58.468 --> 00:02:01.268
Add filters, make the heading row bold, and

45
00:02:01.268 --> 00:02:02.108
give it a little color.

46
00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:05.728
Freeze one row, then widen the columns so

47
00:02:05.728 --> 00:02:07.408
the next actions are readable.

48
00:02:08.088 --> 00:02:10.228
Keep the review status until you decide what

49
00:02:10.228 --> 00:02:10.848
happens next.

50
00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:16.328
My example is speaking gigs. Yours might be

51
00:02:16.328 --> 00:02:18.748
clients, referral partners, or sponsors.

52
00:02:19.408 --> 00:02:22.188
Keep the method, swap in your ideal lead

53
00:02:22.188 --> 00:02:23.028
and your offer.

54
00:02:24.233 --> 00:02:25.519
Here is the next step.

55
00:02:26.139 --> 00:02:29.119
Turn one researched lead into a draft proposal.

56
00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:30.779
Ask for a short message,

57
00:02:31.059 --> 00:02:32.839
check its claims, and revise it.

58
00:02:33.199 --> 00:02:34.119
Keep it as a draft.

59
00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:36.339
You review it before anything sends.

60
00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:39.994
The list is your starting point.

61
00:02:40.514 --> 00:02:41.934
The relationship comes next.

62
00:02:42.454 --> 00:02:44.174
You'll find the full prompts on the lesson

63
00:02:44.174 --> 00:02:44.514
page.
